Usage: pms2dot [--check-order|--reorder] [-h]
  -h, --help     Print this message.
  --check-order  Reject branches outside bitstring-vector order.
  --reorder      Sort branches into bitstring-vector order.
The program receives progress measures ending with '|' via stdin. Each
progress measure is a comma-separated sequence of bitstrings. The
bitstring order is infinite-binary-tree DFS order (0 beta < e < 1 beta);
vectors are compared lexicographically.
